<title>FRANCE: PSA Peugeot Citroen H1 profit falls.</title>
<headline>PSA Peugeot Citroen H1 profit falls.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net attributable			     602  vs	   1,216</p>
<p>    Operating margin			   1,336  vs	   2,776</p>
<p>    Pre-tax					  834  vs	   1,805</p>
<p>    Cashflow				     6,660  vs	   8,080</p>
<p>    Investments				  5,294  vs	   5,425</p>
<p>    Debt					   5,649  vs	   5,509</p>
<p>    Turnover				    89,037  vs	  86,431</p>
<p>NOTE - PSA Peugeot Citroen gave its results in a statement.</p>
<p>It said weakness in several European currencies relative to the French franc had a negative 300 million franc impact on the first-half operating margin compared with the first half of 1995.</p>
<p>It said sales growth reflected an improvement in the product mix and an increase in the group's market share of the upper mid-sized car segment.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
